# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) to run the two checks that touch a LIVE
# endpoint: tests/check_probe.py (AC-9) and the live half of tests/check_id.py
# (AC-4). Every other check in the suite runs offline against the stub server
# in tests/lib/stub_provider.py and needs nothing here.
#
# Loaded by tests/lib/env_local.py, which FILLS GAPS ONLY: a name already set
# in the real environment always wins over this file, so CI's values are never
# replaced and a one-off override (MT_MODEL=other-model uv run ... check_id)
# takes effect.
#
# The skip-vs-fail contract, per section E of the build order:
#   no file, or MT_BASE_URL / MT_MODEL empty  -> both checks exit 3 (SKIP) with
#                                                a named reason, and run_all
#                                                records them as skipped
#   MT_REQUIRE_LIVE=1                         -> every skip is promoted to a
#                                                failure; this is what the
#                                                sign-off run sets
#   MT_NO_ENV_LOCAL=1                         -> this file is not read at all,
#                                                which is how a box that HAS
#                                                credentials reproduces CI's
#                                                skip path
#
# Sign-off run:  MT_REQUIRE_LIVE=1 uv run --project sidecar python tests/run_all.py

# Required. An OpenAI-compatible base URL, including the version segment.
MT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1

# Optional, and may be empty: a local llama.cpp or Ollama server needs no key.
MT_API_KEY=

# Required, and must be VISION-CAPABLE -- check_probe paints a token into an
# image and asserts the model reads it back.
MT_MODEL=
